      <div purpose="landing-page-section">
        <div purpose="section-heading">
          <h2>Built for Windows-first and mixed-fleet teams</h2>
          <p>Whether you manage 500 Windows laptops or 50,000, Fleet gives Windows admins the depth Windows devices require and the cross-platform reach the rest of the business needs.</p>
        </div>
        <div purpose="feature-row">
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Zero touch, $0</h5>
            <p>Your hardware provider installs Fleet before each PC ships, so devices arrive ready and enroll the first time they’re online. No Autopilot, Entra ID P1, or Intune required.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Microsoft Entra ID and Autopilot support</h5>
            <p>Prefer Entra ID? Connect Fleet to <a href="/guides/windows-mdm-setup#step-2-connect-fleet-to-microsoft-entra-id">Entra ID</a> so end users self-enroll the first time they sign in, or layer Fleet onto Autopilot. Both need a per-user Entra ID P1 license. IdP identities map to hosts automatically.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>BitLocker disk encryption</h5>
            <p>Enforce BitLocker, escrow recovery keys to Fleet, and verify encryption status across every Windows device from one dashboard.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Windows OS settings and CSPs</h5>
            <p>Apply OS settings and configuration profiles through <a href="/guides/creating-windows-csps">Windows Configuration Service Providers</a>. Describe the setting you want, and AI drafts the CSP for your review.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Software and patching</h5>
            <p>Deploy Fleet-maintained apps, Microsoft Store apps, and custom packages. Self-service installs keep users moving without tickets.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Windows Update enforcement</h5>
            <p>Set deadlines and grace periods for OS updates. Track install state across every device without waiting on a check-in cycle.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Live reports for every Windows device</h5>
            <p>Powered by osquery, Fleet surfaces hardware, software, patch state, and security posture in seconds, not on the next inventory cycle.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>CIS Benchmarks for Windows</h5>
            <p>Run the complete Windows CIS Benchmark out of the box. Track compliance continuously and remediate with policies.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Scripts, lock, and wipe</h5>
            <p>Run PowerShell scripts on demand from the Fleet UI or API. Remotely lock or wipe lost or compromised Windows devices.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="landing-page-section">
        <div purpose="feature-with-image">
          <div purpose="feature-text">
            <h3>Get AI working for you</h3>
            <p>Fleet works natively with your team’s AI tools, like Copilot, Claude, or any AI harness. Say what you need done. AI proposes the change, and a person on your team approves it before it touches a device. Practice it live at a <a href="/gitops-workshop">free workshop</a> and get certified.</p>
            <div purpose="checklist">
              <p>Configure Windows and third-party apps with prompts like “Disable camera in Firefox.”</p>
              <p>Ask your PCs what’s patched and what’s compliant, and get answers in seconds.</p>
              <p>Review every change before it ships, and undo any mistake.</p>
              <p>Change Windows and Mac settings together, in one request.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-demo">
            <teams-chat-graphic></teams-chat-graphic>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="landing-page-section">
        <div purpose="section-heading">
          <h2>How Fleet is different from Intune and other Windows MDMs</h2>
          <p>Microsoft Intune covers Windows. Fleet covers Windows the same way, then adds the things Intune structurally can’t: AI-native changes with human review, zero touch without a Microsoft license, live osquery data, real cross-platform parity, and an open source codebase you can run on your own infrastructure.</p>
        </div>
        <div purpose="feature-row">
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>AI with a human in the loop</h5>
            <p>Ask for a change to Windows policies, BitLocker settings, or Windows Update deadlines. AI drafts it, and your team reviews it before any device sees it.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Live osquery, not cached check-ins</h5>
            <p>Ask any Windows device a question right now and get an answer in seconds. Patch state, installed software, processes, and BitLocker status are live, not stale.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Same depth across macOS and Linux</h5>
            <p>Manage <a href="/windows">Windows</a>, <a href="/apple">Macs</a>, and <a href="/linux">Linux servers</a> with the same API, the same policies, and the same dashboard. No second tool for the other half of your fleet.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Open source and self-hostable</h5>
            <p><a href="/lp/open-source">Fleet is MIT-licensed</a>. Audit the code, run it in your own VPC, or use Fleet Cloud with 100% feature parity. No Microsoft cloud dependency.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Remote lock for Windows</h5>
            <p>Unlike Intune, Fleet lets you lock Windows 10 and 11 devices to cut off access fast when someone leaves or during a security incident.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Scope transparency for end users</h5>
            <p>Fleet does not collect keystrokes, screen contents, or personal files. <a href="/transparency">See exactly what Fleet can and cannot see</a> on a managed Windows device.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="landing-page-section">
        <div purpose="section-heading">
          <h2>Windows MDM frequently asked questions</h2>
        </div>
        <div purpose="faq" class="d-flex flex-column">
          <div purpose="accordion" class="d-flex flex-column justify-content-start">
            <div purpose="accordion-body">
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="win-faq__header1" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#win-faq__body1" aria-controls="win-faq__body1">
                  What is Windows MDM?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="win-faq__body1" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="win-faq__header1">
                  Windows mobile device management (MDM) is the software and protocols IT teams use to enroll, configure, secure, and report on Windows 10 and Windows 11 devices at scale. A Windows MDM platform applies settings through Windows Configuration Service Providers (CSPs), enforces disk encryption with BitLocker, distributes software and OS updates, and reports back on device posture. Fleet does this across Windows, macOS, Linux, iOS, iPadOS, Android, and ChromeOS from a single open source platform.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="win-faq__header2" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#win-faq__body2" aria-controls="win-faq__body2">
                  Does Fleet replace Microsoft Intune?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="win-faq__body2" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="win-faq__header2">
                  Yes. Fleet covers the core Windows MDM workload that Intune handles: device enrollment, configuration profiles, BitLocker disk encryption, Windows Update enforcement, software deployment, and compliance reporting. Fleet adds AI-native changes with human review, zero touch without a Microsoft license, live osquery data instead of cached check-ins, an open source codebase you can self-host, and the same depth of management for macOS, Linux, iOS, iPadOS, Android, and ChromeOS. Teams typically migrate from Intune to consolidate onto a single cross-platform tool. See the <a href="/guides/windows-mdm-setup#automatic-windows-mdm-migration">Windows MDM migration guide</a> for the process.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="win-faq__header3" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#win-faq__body3" aria-controls="win-faq__body3">
                  Can Fleet manage Windows and macOS together?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="win-faq__body3" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="win-faq__header3">
                  Yes. Fleet manages <a href="/apple">macOS</a>, <a href="/linux">Linux</a>, Windows, iOS, iPadOS, Android, and ChromeOS from a single console, with the same API, the same AI-native workflow, and the same policy engine. You can change Windows and macOS settings together, in one request.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="win-faq__header4" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#win-faq__body4" aria-controls="win-faq__body4">
                  Which versions of Windows does Fleet support?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="win-faq__body4" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="win-faq__header4">
                  Fleet supports Windows 10 and Windows 11 for full MDM enrollment, configuration, BitLocker enforcement, software management, and Windows Update control. Fleet also provides osquery-based visibility, vulnerability reporting, and remote script execution on Windows Server.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="win-faq__header5" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#win-faq__body5" aria-controls="win-faq__body5">
                  How does Fleet enroll Windows devices?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="win-faq__body5" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="win-faq__header5">
                  Fleet supports both manual enrollment and automatic (zero-touch) enrollment for Windows. For zero touch, Fleet gives you an order email. Forward it to Dell, Lenovo, or HP, and they install Fleet before the PC ships. No Autopilot, Entra ID P1, or Intune is required for that path. Alternatively, connect Fleet to Microsoft Entra ID so new devices self-enroll the first time the end user signs in, or use Windows Autopilot. Both of those alternatives require a per-user Entra ID P1 license. The full setup process is documented in the <a href="/guides/windows-mdm-setup">Windows MDM setup guide</a>.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="win-faq__header9" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#win-faq__body9" aria-controls="win-faq__body9">
                  Do I need Autopilot to use Fleet?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="win-faq__body9" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="win-faq__header9">
                  No. Autopilot requires Microsoft Entra ID, and with Fleet, zero-touch setup is simpler. Forward the order email from Fleet to Dell, Lenovo, or HP, and every new PC arrives already managed by Fleet. Customers run thousands of PCs with Fleet and no Autopilot. If you already have Entra and want to keep it, Fleet fully supports Autopilot too. See <a href="/articles/autopilot-without-autopilot">Autopilot without Autopilot</a>.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="win-faq__header10" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#win-faq__body10" aria-controls="win-faq__body10">
                  What Microsoft license does zero-touch setup need?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="win-faq__body10" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="win-faq__header10">
                  None. Just forward the email from Fleet to Dell, Lenovo, or HP. You only need Microsoft Entra ID P1 if you choose Entra automatic enrollment or Autopilot.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="win-faq__header6" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#win-faq__body6" aria-controls="win-faq__body6">
                  How does Fleet handle BitLocker on Windows?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="win-faq__body6" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="win-faq__header6">
                  Fleet enforces BitLocker disk encryption on Windows devices, escrows the recovery keys, and reports encryption status across the fleet. Recovery keys are retrievable through the Fleet UI or REST API, and BitLocker state is visible alongside every other device attribute on the host details page.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="win-faq__header7" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#win-faq__body7" aria-controls="win-faq__body7">
                  Is Fleet open source?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="win-faq__body7" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="win-faq__header7">
                  Yes. The majority of Fleet is released under the MIT license, and all of Fleet's source code is public on GitHub at <a href="https://github.com/fleetdm/fleet" target="_blank">github.com/fleetdm/fleet</a>. A separate set of paid features lives in an <code>/ee</code> directory under a commercial license. See the <a href="/lp/open-source">open source MDM page</a> for the full breakdown.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="win-faq__header8" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#win-faq__body8" aria-controls="win-faq__body8">
                  Can Fleet be self-hosted?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="win-faq__body8" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="win-faq__header8">
                  Yes. Fleet can be deployed <a href="/lp/on-premise">on-premises</a>, in any major cloud (AWS, Azure, GCP, DigitalOcean), in containers (Docker, or Kubernetes via Helm or Terraform), or in air-gapped environments. Teams that prefer a managed option can choose Fleet Cloud and get the same Windows MDM features either way.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="d-flex flex-row justify-content-start">
              <p purpose="contact-note">Have another question? <a href="/docs/get-started/faq">Read the full FAQ</a> or <a href="/contact">talk to an engineer</a>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
